<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Sept 20.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Sept 20.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 09/20/96  09/13/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    191.71    183.87    83.07	79.68     84.40</p>
<p>West	    226.45    222.26    80.82	80.39     90.30</p>
<p>Total Canada  418.17    406.13    81.84	80.06     87.40</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 09/20/96: 230.77 bcf, 09/13/96: 230.77 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 09/20/96: 280.19 bcf, 09/13/96: 276.49 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. -- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
